hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"151","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi told us, Khalaf bin Al-Walid told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Amir bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Shaqiq bin Salamah, on the authority of Uthman ibn Affan said, “He performed ablution, washed his face three times, sniffed the nose three times, rinsed his mouth three times, and wiped the outsides of his head and ears.” And their inner parts, and his feet three times, and he mixed his beard and the toes of his feet, and said: This is how I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performing ablution."
"152","Ishaq bin Mansour told us, Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Mahdi, told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Amer bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Shaqiq bin Salamah, he said: I saw Uthman bin Affan. He performed ablution, washed his hands three times, rinsed his mouth and nose, washed his face three times, and wiped his ears. Their outer and inner parts, and he washed his feet three times, and combed his fingers, and combed his beard when he washed his face three times, and said: I saw the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he did as you saw me do. Abdul Rahman said: He mentioned his hands reaching to the elbows, and I do not know how he mentioned it. Abu Bakr said: This is Amer bin Shaqiq, the son of Hamza al-Asadi, and Shaqiq bin Salamah is Abu Wael."
